// ══ THE CROWD FIRES (BOOK II #421) — ONE GRAMMAR, FOUR FAMILIES ═══════════════════════════════════
//   **THE DIRECTOR'S RULING, 2026-08-14: *"dont allow my shit to be capped … EVERYTHING IS SO FUCKING
//   MILD ITS ANNOYING."*** Shown four family fire-ceilings he chose SCALE WITH THE CROWD over killing
//   them outright. Four ceilings were confirmed live before a line was written: the priesthood's
//   `fireN`/`beamN` 2, the wolf pack's shared 0.7s release clock, the cloud's `VOLLEY_RATE` 4 with
//   `MAX_POP_BULLETS` 20, and the street's `focusF` `Math.min(8, …)` plus `jackBreath`.
//
//   ⚠ **THE ORDER FORBIDS THE OBVIOUS FIX BY NAME: *"`fireN: 2` becoming `fireN: 8` is the same crime
//   with a bigger number."*** So the shape here is not a bigger constant, and it is not four separate
//   inventions either — four families getting louder by four different rules is unreadable even when
//   every one is survivable, which is this stone's own named silent risk.
//
//   **THE SHAPE: A SHARE OF THE LIVE CROWD, FLOORED AT TODAY'S NUMBER, NEVER CEILINGED.**
//   `Math.max` and `Math.ceil` only — **there is deliberately no `Math.min` in this function**, and its
//   absence is the whole point. Grep it: a clamp reintroduced here re-caps all four families at once.
//
//   **WHY A SHARE, derived from what a pilot can READ rather than from a number that felt safe** (the
//   order's own instruction). A pilot cannot count 104 rabbis and has never once tried. What they CAN
//   read is a proportion — *about one in eight of them is winding up right now* — and a proportion is
//   the same sentence at 3 bodies and at 104, which is exactly what a constant is not. A constant says
//   "two of them are shooting", which is a true and terrifying sentence at 3 and a comic one at 104:
//   **the priesthood has been delivering identical fire at 104 as at 3.**
//
//   **WHY THE OLD NUMBER SURVIVES AS A FLOOR AND WHY THAT IS NOT THE CRIME.** The floor is what makes
//   this safe to ship uncapped: below the crossover every family behaves EXACTLY as it does today, so
//   the early waves, the whole STORY mode and every sandbox fixture are unchanged by construction
//   rather than by testing. The named crime is a bigger CEILING — `fireN: 8` would make wave 3 harder
//   AND still cap wave 21. A floor does neither. Nothing here can ever return less than it does today.
//
//   **WHAT THIS CANNOT SEE (THE HUMILITY CLAUSE):** it is arithmetic on a count and knows nothing about
//   whether the result is READABLE, survivable, or fun. It cannot see the screen, cannot tell 13
//   simultaneous beams from 13 staggered ones, and has no opinion on which of the four families
//   dominates the frame when all four scale at once. That is measured in the log and graded by eye.
// ══ (#530) THE SHOW RISES WITH THE CROWD — floor-not-lid, one rule, crossover ~700 bodies ══════════
//   His complaint is about the DRAW: at 2,100 bodies every cosmetic pool saturates on a fraction of the
//   field, so most of his fight is unpainted. Each pool keeps its shipped number as a FLOOR and grows
//   linearly past it — so every wave he plays today is BYTE-IDENTICAL and only the flood sees more.
//   ⚠ NOT `crowdShare`: that one now multiplies by `wmapAgg()` (#526, the AGGRESSION axis), and a
//   spectacle ceiling must not inherit a difficulty multiplier. Same idiom, separate organ, on purpose.
function spectacle(floor, share) { return Math.max(floor, Math.ceil(enemies.length * share)); }
// ══ THE QUALITY TIERS (stone 26) — HIS ORDER: *"graphics should have low medium high and that should be a
//    stone, or maybe a few stones that will let people with shitier machines play the game by lower vfx to
//    bass level. will be important in higher waves. this is not joke of a project to keep in ind."*
//
//  **HIGH IS THE DEFAULT AND THE REFERENCE, AND IT IS PIXEL-IDENTICAL BY CONSTRUCTION.** `qShare` returns
