  //   would have governed is a SPAWN BOUND (`live < spectacle(LABDEATH.CAP, 0.04)`), not a trim — so
  //   gating it would shift the seeded stream (trap #395). **A registry row for something that is not
  //   actually gated is the exact rot this registry exists to prevent**, so the row came out with it.
  floaters:   { med: 1.0, low: 1.0 },   // MESSAGES ARE NOT DECORATION — registered so it is a RULING and not an omission
  loottrail:  { med: 0.6, low: 0.3 },   // (FREE PASS 1/5) the loot-trail ring pool — a ceiling, not a budget
  strikearc:  { med: 0.6, low: 0.3 },   // (G10B) the sword's strike lightning — an ARRAY TRIM on strikeArcs, cap 8
  swordkillfx: { med: 0.6, low: 0.3 },  // (dress pass, 2026-09-01) the sword's X-of-steel kill marks — an ARRAY TRIM, cap 8
  // ══ THE CLASSIFICATION SWEEP (stone two). Nine more rows, one per decorative pool, every one an ARRAY
  //    TRIM. The sweep read EVERY `.shift()` in the file — 32 pools — and ruled on each; the ones that are
  //    NOT here are listed with their reasons in `QNOT` below, because the registry's teeth can only bite a
  //    pool somebody classified.
