//   MEASURED FIRST (`tools/_stone11_survives.js`): with 9,000 in his pocket, EVERY door read 0 after --
//   a run abandoned, a run died in, mode select, a story retry, a whole bell-to-bell run. **`restart()`
//   zeroes `diamondsSpent` and calls `seedGems()`, which zeroes `gemsTaken`, and the balance is those two
//   subtracted.** So merging the purses alone delivered nothing a player could feel: money still could
//   not walk out of a run, it was destroyed on the way.
//   **THIS KEEPS THE WALLET ACROSS THE TWO WAVE-SIDE DOORS ONLY, and that is a scope line, not timidity.**
//   The STORY retry (`runItBack`, the death-screen ENTER) still starts a mission at zero exactly as it
//   always has -- his order is *"one wallet everywhere"* about the two SHOPS, and the street's own
//   restart rules are his to change, not mine to assume.
//   ⚠ **WHY THE STORY RETRY IS NOT TOUCHED, WITH THE REASON NAMED: `seedGems()` REBUILDS THE WHOLE GEM
//   FIELD.** Persist the balance across a story restart and the street becomes an infinite fountain --
//   restart, re-collect the same field, repeat. That is a DESIGN ruling with his name on it (and a save
//   key it does not have; `dreamsim2 [VK]` guards new vault keys deliberately). It is on `QUESTIONS.md`.
//   ⚠ **IT IS A HOLD/RELEASE PAIR AND NOT A `walletKeep(restart)` WRAPPER, BECAUSE A LAW READS THIS
//   SOURCE.** The wrapper shipped first and `mirrorsim [RL]` convicted it: *"`toModeSelect()` no longer
//   calls `restart()` in its first lines. That call is the link that carries `restart()`'s `invuln = 0`
//   to every door out of the sandbox."* The behaviour was identical -- the wrapper does call it -- but a
//   source-text law that cannot see the call is a guard that has lost its subject, and the guard is right
//   about the class it catches. **The CODE moved back to the law's shape rather than the law being
//   loosened to accept a wrapper**, which is the cheaper of the two and keeps the teeth exactly.
