// rising at 50px/s, and governed by THE CROWD LAW — twelve live, de-overlapped at 26px, a note with no room
// dies rather than overlap. Criterion B's guard shipped long before this stone.
//   **BUT A CAP ALONE WOULD EAT HIS WAVE TEN.** At 267 bodies a twelve-note ceiling means simultaneous
// payments are evicted in silence — paid and not told, which is a worse lie than the column was. So a reward
// landing on a live one MERGES into it and re-kicks it, exactly as `styleCall`'s burst collapse turns a
// repeated call into a climbing ladder in place.
//   **THE MERGE RADIUS IS NOT A TASTE NUMBER — IT IS THE CROWD LAW'S OWN COLLISION TEST, REUSED**:
// `|dx| * 2 < w1 + w2` over `w = text.length * 10 + 16`. Two rewards merge exactly when they would otherwise
// have collided and one would have been pushed down or killed. Chosen by arithmetic, not by taste — and the
