// ---- THE BEAT IS A FOURTH `dil` SOURCE AND NOT A CLOCK (criterion B) --------------------------------
// THE ORDER SAYS "A THIRD `dil` SOURCE" AND THE CHAIN ALREADY HAS THREE: the apex hang (0.35), the veil
// (`SMOKE_DIL` 0.45) and #109's TIME SLOW (`slowDil()`, 0.50), which landed after the order was written.
// So this is the FOURTH term, and it goes at the HEAD of the chain rather than the tail — #109's own
// comment rules precedence by depth and by authorship ("a stunt outranks a purchase"), and a scripted
// death beat outranks a stunt: it is the one moment in this game the author is speaking rather than the
// pilot. It is also the deepest, which keeps the chain ordered by depth from head to tail.
//   THE CEREMONY'S OWN CLOCK IS A REFEREE (`rdt`), and that is not decoration. On the world's `dt` the
// beat would advance at its own dilation — 1.7s of ceremony would take 9.4 REAL seconds at 0.18x, and
// the deeper the dial the longer the hold, so the ONE dial a tuner would reach for would silently move
// two things. That is the class the RDT doctrine was written for, and `rdt` is the shipped token for it.
const MIRDEATH = {
  LEN: 1.7,     // the whole ceremony, in REAL seconds
  CATCH: 0.5,   // how long the deepest hold lasts before the world starts coming back — real seconds
  DIL: 0.18,    // the world's factor during the catch: deeper than the hang (0.35), the veil (0.45) and TIME SLOW (0.50)
  MOOD: 900,    // the mix ceiling while the catch holds: under TIME SLOW's 1100, over the veil's 720 — four moments, four sounds
};
