  const side = i % 2 ? 1 : -1;
  // ══ (#507) TWO TOWERS — THE INDEX USED TO MARCH OFF THE END OF THE WORLD ═══════════════════════
  //   `i * 35` is a distance, and the street is 13,152px of clamp window. At his wave 22 the drone
  //   count is 2,000, so the fan asks for 70,000px of room. MEASURED on the live tree before the
  //   cure, pilot mid-street: **the clamp first bites at index 163, and 1,837 of 2,000 bodies land on
  //   exactly TWO POINTS — 918 on the left wall, 919 on the right — 165 distinct positions in all.**
  //   Nothing is lost and it resolves (`wrunStragglers` pulls anything past 1,400px at up to 600px/s,
  //   so the field converges in ~11s), which is exactly why no law ever caught it: the census counts
  //   and the timing are all correct. **But the opening seconds of the wave he built for spectacle
  //   are two towers of drones rather than a sky.**
  //   ⚠ **THE CURE IS DISTRIBUTION, NOT A LIMIT, AND THE SHAPE IS `lionDy`'s** — that function already
  //   solves this for altitude by deriving its step from the count and wrapping (`i % N`), and a second
  //   scheme here would be the parallel THE PRIOR ART LAW names. `wrunEdgeX` is not handed the count,
  //   so the room itself supplies it: measure how many steps fit between the door and the wall ON THIS
  //   SIDE, wrap the index into that many slots, and offset each successive lap by a QUARTER STEP so
  //   the laps interleave instead of stacking. Four laps before any position repeats exactly, and the
  //   existing ±200 jitter rides on top.
  //   ⚠ **EVERY INDEX BELOW `slots` IS BYTE-IDENTICAL TO WHAT SHIPPED**, which is what keeps the four
  //   laws that pin this function green: `suisim [GP]` clause 3 (arrival spread, N=8 — and its own text
  //   says step 35 exists "precisely so every other family stays byte-identical"), `rabbisim`'s
  //   `i % 2` edge parity for WEB BREAKER and CALLED THE FEINT (parity reads the RAW `i`, untouched
  //   below), and `wavesim [38]`'s corner flip at `i % 10`. The wrap can only ever fire where the old
  //   code was already pinning bodies to a wall.
  const st = step || 35;
