// THE EXPORTED BELL (D181, stone 136, v1.6.515) — **WHY THE BELL'S WAIT-LIST IS A FUNCTION AND NOT FIVE
// BOOLEANS INLINE.** It returns the REASON the wave is not over, or `''` when it is.
//
// THE CASE, and it is on the record because this shift filed it as its own counsel two stones ago: seating a
// boss at wave 30 turned `wavesim [IH2]` red **on a working game**. `[IH2]` rings the bell by sweeping the
// field, and it swept the three things the bell waited on THE DAY IT WAS WRITTEN. The bell had since grown a
// fourth — `duelling`, at #95 — and the law walks the climb from wave 1 to V7's roof, so it cannot skip 30.
// **A law that reproduces a condition LIST is correct the day it is written and silently incomplete forever
// after.** Neither that law nor `[SP1]` was findable by grepping for `30`, because neither names it.
//
// SO THE LIST LIVES HERE, ONCE, AND EVERY READER READS IT. That is `prizeStage()`'s doctrine — the one this
// file argues for at length — applied to a condition list instead of a stage. The fifth condition, whenever it
// comes, lands on this function and `[IH2]` inherits it without being edited.
