  //   variants carry non-1.0 `rich` (0.25 on V18 to 2.4 on V23) and `rewardM` runs 0.5 to 2.5. It is kept
  //   rather than deleted because the MECHANISM it describes is exactly right and is what #211 measured
  //   against — only the "ships at 1.0 across the board" sentence has rotted. Measured consequence:
  //   band 1 on V23 pays ◆1.334 against `[F49b]`s ◆1.25 ceiling, which that law cannot see because it
  //   never starts a run and so always reads `rich` = 1. Published in `ECONOMY.md`, not tuned here.
  // THE ORIGINAL NOTE, PRESERVED: Every variant carries `rich: 1.0`
