//
// **CLAUSE B IS RULED, NOT FIXED: THE SCORCH IS GROUND-ONLY, IN WORDS.** The ellipse anchors to
// `groundY()` regardless of what the body died on, so a rooftop kill marks the street below it. Taking
// the platform is `washFloor`'s idiom and it is a real change to four producers, three of which do not
// know what they were standing on. **The ruling: a scorch is a mark on the GROUND, and a body that dies
// in the air leaves its mark where its wreck lands** — which is exactly what `wrecksTick` already does,
// pushing the scar at the impact rather than at the kill. The one producer that can genuinely mark a
// roof is the rabbi's beam, and it is throttled theater. A later stone that wants roof scorch takes the
