  // **`won`, THROUGH THE ONE DOOR — AND `drawsim [FCK]` TAUGHT ME THE DESIGN BY REDDING.** The first cut
  //   wrote `FORGE.state = 'die'` here and `'off'` at the end, and the law counted FOUR writers against
  //   its two: *"a third writer is how a fifth state gets invented."* It was right and the fifth state
  //   was mine — `forgeClockSet` already carries `won`, which is what `notes/FORGE-ARC.md` beat 4a calls
  //   this moment in as many words (*"THE SHATTER — win"*). Its guard is this call's own precondition:
  //   only a RUNNING fight can end, and `forgeDamage` refuses unless the state is `run`.
  forgeClockSet('won');
  FORGE.shards = forgeShatter();
