  //   corpse's geometry and a laid mark would still bite a pilot after the thing that aimed it is gone.
  //   `mirrorDeathBegin`'s *"a dead man does not close his tab"* aimed forward, which is what it is for.
  FORGE.arcs.length = 0; FORGE.marks.length = 0;
  FORGE.breakT = 0; FORGE.iT = 0; FORGE.strikeCd = 0; FORGE.curtainCd = 0;
  rings.push({ x: FORGE.X, y: groundY() - FORGE.ALT, age: 0, life: 0.8, maxR: FORGE.SPAN * 2.2, color: '#dff2ff', wd: 5 });
  // ══ THE PAYOUT (#167), WRITTEN AT THE SHATTER SOURCE AND NOWHERE ELSE. `notes/FORGE-MATH.md` §4 rules
  //  this exact seat — *"the payout is written at the shatter source, inside `forgeShatter()`, beside
  //  `sealTear()`'s own idiom, and NEVER at a banking door"* — and it lists the five wallet-credit
  //  writers so the building stone cannot reach one by accident. This reaches none of them: the bullion
  //  banks through the shipped gem-pickup door (`g.bundle ? g.worth : 1`) with no new writer at all, and
  //  the shine rides `styleCall`'s own tap. **Nothing is minted here.**
  //  Seated in `forgeDeathBegin` rather than `forgeShatter` because that one is a pure geometry factory
  //  called for its return value — paying from it would mint on every call, and `[SHT]` clause 2 calls it
  //  directly to count pieces. This is the door §4 means: the one place the death actually happens.
  // ══ THE VERDICT (BOOK II #169) — **THE WIN SAID NOTHING AT ALL, AND THAT IS A COUNT:** grepping
  //  `forgeDeathBegin` for `lane: 'announce'` returned **0**. Four stones built this moment — its picture,
  //  its voice, its payout — and the announcer never once named it. The LOSS has said two things since
  //  #143 and #168 (`THE FORGE IS GONE`, and the price receipt); the win was mute.
  //
  //  **`pr: 3` IS THE CEREMONY SEAT AND IT IS TAKEN DELIBERATELY**, which is criterion A. `TEAR SEALED`'s
  //  own note is the rule: *the seal is the POINT of the event — it must not lose its seat to the kill
  //  calls it caused.* A forge win spills a bank of bullion and every piece is a kill call waiting to
  //  happen; without the top seat the announcer would report the change and swallow the reason for it.
  //
  //  **THE SHAPE IS `THE SKY HOLDS`'s, AND SO IS THE LENGTH — READ, NOT TYPED.** `notes/FORGE-ARC.md` §3
  //  derived `FORGE.SHATTER = 2.6 s` *verbatim from that floater's own `__life: 2.6`*, so the line's life
  //  is `FORGE_DIE.LEN`: the words are on screen for exactly as long as the body takes to come apart,
  //  and re-tuning the ceremony carries its own caption along instead of leaving it hanging over an
  //  empty sky or vanishing mid-fall.
  //
  //  **THE TEXT IS RULED HERE BECAUSE NO DOC NAMES IT.** `FORGE-ARC` and `FORGE-SOUND` both derive FROM
  //  `THE SKY HOLDS` and neither writes the forge's own words. Rejected: anything shaped like the loss.
  //  `THE FORGE IS GONE` is what the pilot reads when the timer wins, so a win phrased as an absence
  //  (*BROKEN*, *DOWN*, *NO MORE*) is the one thing this line may not be — criterion B's *the loss must
  //  not sound like a win* has a mirror, and it is that the win must not READ like the loss. Possession
  //  is the opposite of absence, and `THE INGOT` is the body's own display name in three shipped docs.
  floaters.push({ lane: 'announce', pr: 3, x: FORGE.X, y: groundY() - FORGE.ALT - 220, text: FORGE_WIN_LINE, age: 0, big: true, gold: true, kinetic: 2, __life: FORGE_DIE.LEN });
