  //    Eight seams grow from the girdle's centre outward at `crackU`, clipped to the silhouette so they
  //    are splits IN the stone rather than lines over it. **FILLED TAPERED QUADS, NEVER STROKES** —
  //    `MIRSHARD`'s rule: the draw recorder logs `fill()` and is blind to `stroke()`, so a stroked crack
  //    would be invisible to every law in this building. **ZERO DICE:** the angles come off a hash of the
  //    seam INDEX and nothing else, because `Math.random()` at draw time is the seeded world stream and
  //    this file's own arc block records what borrowing it cost (THE TWO STREAMS LAW). A crack that
  //    moved between frames would not be a crack.
