    //   the altitude. It has to be glued to where this thing is so I can easily find it even when it's on screen. It
    //   has to be pointing at it."*) ONE pointer grammar for every live wound in the theater, queued here and painted
    //   in the HUD pass (v1.6.1348's lesson stands: a world-pass arrow gets buried by the stage's later layers). ON
    //   FRAME the arrow hangs GLUED over the wound's top lip and points down at its center; OFF FRAME it sits on the
    //   frame's rail where the line from the screen's center to the wound leaves the screen, ROTATED along that line.
    //   Both carry the altitude readout: the wound's dy against the pilot's own. The two fixed arrows this replaces —
