    //   put the heat on `k²`, which is 0.014 alpha by the time anybody is looking at the site — so the
    //   reader got a neutral charcoal stroke and said so: *"it has no colour relationship to the event …
    //   a scar left by a green hole in the sky should carry green"*, and *"it crosses the sun bloom, a
    //   white cloud and blue sky and stays the same flat grey through all three — that flat-across-all-
    //   backgrounds behaviour is exactly what a debug stroke looks like."* Both are one fault: the pigment
    //   was gone. The core now carries `TEARVIEW.GLOW`, the same green the window was, and it fades WITH
    //   the wound instead of ahead of it.
    ctx.beginPath();
    for (let yy = t52; yy <= b52; yy += 18) ctx.lineTo(sc.x + wob52(yy), yy);
