// ===== THE DELTA (BOOK II #320) — "the old number, the new number" =====
//   The director, `THE-HUNDRED` 4.10: *"At the moment of buying, show the upgrade against the one he already
//   has: the old number, the new number. Player notices: he stops buying a rung that is worse than the rung
//   he owns."* Every vendor ladder in this file already carries `vals[]` and `lv` — the numbers existed all
//   along and simply were never shown. The boards printed an ADJECTIVE (*"fast landings blast the ground
//   HARDER"*) where they could have printed `0 → 11`.
//   **THESE ARE TOP-LEVEL ON PURPOSE.** `drawAuraBoard` is nested inside the draw path, and a law that has to
//   parse a painter to check arithmetic is a law testing implementation. A law can call these.
//   **`unit` AND `zeroOff` EXIST BECAUSE OF FOUR ROWS, NOT ONE.** The order names `reflex` (`[0, 4, 2.5]`,
//   where 0 is OFF and lower is better) as the case that lets a pilot buy what looks like a downgrade. A
//   sweep of every ladder found **FOUR** that descend: `reflex`, `arate` (FASTER HANDS), `coils` (FAST
//   RECOVERY) and `vrefill`. All four are CLOCKS, and a bare `4 → 2.5` on any of them reads as a loss. With
//   the unit attached, `4.0s → 2.5s` reads as a clock getting shorter, which is what it is. `arate`'s own
