      //   below says *"crowd it at the WRONG MOMENT"* — which presumes a moment exists to be read. Before
      //   the grace it did not: a shmoopy could be spooked on the frame it arrived, having never completed
      //   one sputter, and 36% of all real arrivals died exactly that way. One full arc is the smallest
      //   window in which the rhythm 2/6 designed can be seen at all, so it is the smallest honest grace.
      //   **It does not make the panic rarer for a pilot who is playing** — 3.2 s of a 14 s life is still
      //   most of it. It stops the family being decided before the pilot has looked at it.
      // ⚠ **HORIZONTAL DISTANCE, NOT 2D — clause 3 caught this and it was a design bug, not a fixture one.**
      //   The panic asks whether something is charging BENEATH it. Measured in 2D the test could never fire:
      //   when it is high (alt 220) a grounded pilot is 180px below it, so a 120px radius is unreachable at
      //   exactly the moment the panic is supposed to exist for. **The pilot rushing UNDER it is the event.**
      // ⚠ **THE PANIC DROP, AND IT IS THE HALF THAT MATTERS.** RUSHING it while it is high is a different
      //   act from catching it, and it must not be a pure fail: it releases the prize as a REAL falling
      //   prize and bolts. **Two gates keep the acts distinct — ALTITUDE and SPEED.** Down in the dip you
