  // real light has a lit side and a dark side, and that contrast is most of what says GEM rather than slab.
  // top, right, bottom, left. ON A NARROW STONE THE TOP AND BOTTOM ARE THE WIDE ENDS — they are the only
  // walls with pixels to spare, so they carry the read: a hot catch-light across the top and a dark base
  // under it. That is the gold bar's treatment, which survives at an even smaller radius than this.
