  // go, hold their edges — and the roundness comes from the bands crowding toward the light, not from a ramp.
  // Six, and the outermost band does NOT go to near-black. At five bands the outer ring is 36% of the
  // stone's whole area, so putting it at the bottom of the range wrapped the ruby in a heavy dark rim and
