// THE SOUND BOARD (ARMORY #22): every registered sound carries its voice in ONE map, applied by the
// wrapper below — the pilot's arsenal on 'weapons', the enemies' war on 'street', movement and
// economy chrome on 'ui'. A sound missing from this map is a FINDING ([D24] sweeps for it).
// THE WAVE VOICES (FULL-SHIFT #7): every screen seam the census called silent gets a short
// chrome voice on the WAVE bus. One-shot UI moments — no density risk beyond the synth's own
// budget; the bell is the biggest sound the mode owns, on purpose.
// THE MILESTONE STINGERS (FULL-SHIFT #8): five signature hits, one per named wave — short,
// distinct, memorable. Each borrows its system's own sound grammar so the ear learns the cast:
// blood's snap, the wall's organ, the priesthood's gold, the tear's sub-bass wrongness, and
// EVERYTHING stacking all of it. Character calls — every design flagged for the pilot's recast.
// THE LOOT SOUNDS (FULL-SHIFT #9): the jewelry counter — a WATCH pops with fine clockwork and
// a counter bell; a CHAIN falls in heavy links. Distinct from the diamond's sine family by
