// **THE LEVEL IS READ FROM THE CENSUS, NOT SET BY EAR** (criterion B): `gallery/stone-ears/INDEX.json` puts
// `wbell` — the wave's biggest moment — at peak -19.08 dBFS at `vol: 0.16`, and `flutter` at -47.60 was
// MEASURED inaudible under a bed. So a clock that must never compete with the bell that ends the wave, nor
// vanish, targets ~-27 dBFS: `0.16 × 10^((-27+19.08)/20) ≈ 0.064`. Arithmetic, then a capture to check it.
//   rung 0 — each MINUTE: a low unhurried stroke, the hour bell of a quiet clock. No edge at all.
//   rung 1 — 0:30: the same stroke higher and shorter, with a thin edge on it.
//   rung 2 — 0:10: highest, shortest, thinnest. The edge is the message.
// `step` is clamped because THE AUDITION calls every voice as `SFX[name](player.x)` — clink's own lesson,
// and a pilot at x=6000 must not be able to ask for rung 6000.
// THE FORGE'S DREAD VOICE (BOOK II #144). **THREE RUNGS AND THEY DESCEND**, which is the whole finding
// `notes/FORGE-SOUND.md` §4 corrected into the doctrine: the shipped `swarm.countdown` grammar reads as
// *"an 880 mark and a tick"* and is actually TWO DIFFERENT VOICES — 880 Hz for 0.12 s, then 660 Hz for
// 0.09 s — so the clock FALLS in pitch as it runs out. The forge's clock is 120 s with three marks, so
// §4 adds a rung ABOVE rather than below: 990 Hz, a third over the shipped 880.
//   `step` is clamped for `tefChime`'s own stated reason: THE AUDITION calls every voice as
//   `SFX[name](player.x)`, and a pilot at x=6000 must not be able to ask for rung 6000.
//   VOL 0.07 IS THE SHIPPED FIGURE, taken verbatim from `swarm.countdown` rather than re-picked — and
//   `notes/HEAR-RIG.md` is explicit that **a `vol` field is not a level**, so the dBFS band is whatever the
//   capture says and is declared as a range, never as a decimal.
// THE FORGE'S ARRIVAL VOICE (BOOK II #147). **CRITERION B IS THE WHOLE DESIGN BRIEF: THE FORGE IS BORN
// 12,000 FT ABOVE THE PILOT AND ITS ARRIVAL IS HEARD BEFORE IT IS EVER SEEN.** `notes/FORGE-SOUND.md` §2's
// band table covers beats 1-5 and has no row for beat 0, so this is a derived number rather than a read
