// GAINING, so it climbs. Two tones a fifth apart plus a low body, on the `wave` bus with its siblings.
// **THE FIRST CUT MEASURED -14.51 dBFS AND THAT IS LOUDER THAN THE SHATTER, WHICH §2 RULES MAY NOT BE
// EXCEEDED.** I derived the band honestly — a step under the shatter's -18..-16 floor, well over `fgWarn`'s
// measured -35.3 — declared **-26..-22**, and then wrote three `vol` arguments that landed nowhere near it.
// `notes/HEAR-RIG.md` says exactly this in four words: **A `vol` FIELD IS NOT A LEVEL.** Three voices summing
