  //   reader measured what that costs on a swarm frame: **24.9% of the entire frame at pure white (>254),
  //   38.3% above 240, and 78.3% of the ground gone in the left half.** *"You cannot see your own character
  //   or the floor you are standing on."* Its diagnosis was exact — *"the failure is unbounded additive
  //   alpha, which a count cap does not touch"* — and this is the answer it asked for.
  //   **THE SHAPE: the budget is spent, not divided.** Each lamp takes what it needs from a fixed pool in
  //   age order, and when the pool is empty the rest contribute nothing. Dividing equally would dim a LONE
  //   blast the moment a second one existed somewhere off-screen; spending means one blast is exactly as
