    //   them.** I wrote `if (give <= 0) break`, which treats an EXPIRED lamp (k = 0, its life run out) as an
    //   exhausted pool and abandons every lamp behind it. A probe counting the calls found **zero lamps
    //   painted on the swarm's peak frame** — the whole ground light silently switched off the moment one
    //   dead entry sat near the front of the array. The frame looked unchanged because it WAS unchanged in
    //   the only way that matters: nothing was lit either way, before or after my "fix".
