  //   converging on one coordinate MUST stack. *"they fan out but when they target they just overlap."*
  //   **THE RULING THE ORDER SAYS THE LEG RESTS ON: FORMATION-LEVEL TRACKING**, and the reason is that the
  //   other two options are the bug. *Homing inside the lane* means every bolt aims at one point, which IS
  //   today's defect wearing a new name. *Outermost lanes only* leaves every inner bolt stacking. So the
  //   FORMATION tracks him and each bolt holds a lateral LANE OFFSET beside the aim line: they fan from the
  //   muzzle, then run parallel, and they cannot restack because their aim points are distinct by
  //   construction. **His tuning ruling is TIGHT** — `PULSE_LANE` 13px, so a six-stream fan spans 65px,
  //   about one body wide: it may cross a body, it never becomes one line.
  //   ⚠ **THE MUZZLE FAN IS NOT TOUCHED.** `bolts` above keeps its exact angles, so `pulselab [F2]`'s
  //   0.036-rad ten-stream pin, `[F1]`'s muzzle poses and `[F3]`'s counts all stand unchanged. This stone
  //   changes WHERE A BOLT AIMS, never where it starts.
