    // **IT WRAPS AT FULL SIZE; IT DOES NOT SHRINK. A COLD READER KILLED THE SHRINK AND THE CODE CONVICTED
    // ITSELF.** The first cut scaled an over-long title down, floored at 8.5px — and this comment's own
    // earlier draft said *"past 9.5px a stand's title stops being a label"*, so the floor shipped a full
    // point below the bar the author had just written. The measured result: PLAQUE VII drew at 9.0px with a
    // 5px cap height while its own grey "E — READ" prompt drew at 11px / 6px cap. **The name of a plaque was
    // smaller than the instruction for reading it**, and the row came out uniform in width and uneven in
    // voice — the exact failure this stone's written direction pre-committed to refusing.
    // The em dash is the honest break because the titles are already built around one: "PLAQUE V" is the
    // number and "SETTER'S NOTE №1" is the name, so the wrap falls on a seam the canon put there. Both
