  //   decoration returned, the frame fell under 20 fps, red again: 35 arm/clear flips in five minutes, period ~7 s - his sentence
  //   "when it goes into the red it all speeds up, then yellow, then slows down again" is that cycle. A guard that clears on the fps
  //   its own arms produced is a limit cycle by construction, so the clear no longer reads fps or the whole frame AT ALL: red holds at
  //   least GOV.HOLD s of wall time, then clears only after GOV.CLR_S s of the THINKING half (GOV.upMs - update()'s own wall time,
  //   the quantity the wiretap's `up` measures) under GOV.CLR_MS ms, because the paint's share is exactly what red removed. The arm is
  //   the shipped one (two seconds under 20 fps on the smoothed gauge). PBUDGET stays 700 both ways (v1.6.679: the guard keeps its
  //   senses and no longer cuts). GAUGE.lowT/okT/fps/dil keep accumulating in frameInner for the readouts; okT simply drives nothing
  //   now. YELLOW's own rung (govTick) is left as it was: it shares the SHAPE of this defect (a rung that clears on the frame its own
  //   arms cheapened) but its arms move the frame by ~1-2 ms against a 12..15 ms dead band, so it cannot self-drive the way red did.
  // THE LATCH HOLE (v1.6.1423). His wiretap of 1422 (2026-09-04 22:03): 0 enemies alive, 39 ghosts, ~3,000 live bolts - the thinking
  //   half was 2-4 ms, so the clear above fired while the PAINT was the wall (the draw half 163 ms mean, 481 worst, off red; 3 ms under
