  // **THE BODY CARRIES A PLATFORM WITH IT (#223), rather than the landing loop learning a second
  // geometry.** `platforms` entries are `{x, w, dy}` measured up from `groundY()`; a breakable is
  // `{x, y, r, h}` measured down from its own feet. Teaching the landing loop both conventions is how a
  // system grows the seam `washFloor` warns about, so instead the breakable MINTS a platform in the
  // shape the loop already speaks, and the loop never learns anything. `desertLand` is the flag
  // `platLandable` looks for -- this is the one kind that may catch a pilot on a flat desert, and it
