    // *A gap tighter than the pen is not a gap* gives the floor of one; the second pen is the same step this
    // room has now paid for twice in three stones (the brush root, the bone) — **a derived floor is the
    // smallest EXPRESSIBLE thing, never the smallest READABLE one.** Measured: `TWEED.R` 16 and `sc` in
    // [0.7, 1.3], so the ball spans 22.4-41.6 world px (19.0-35.4 screen at the shipped WORLD_ZOOM 0.85) on a
    // 1.6 world-px pen. Two pens at the smallest radius is 3.2 / 11.2 = 0.286 rad, and holding the ANGLE fixed
    // means the gap scales with the ball: exactly two pens on the smallest weed, three on the largest.
    //
