//   · the SHADE column is counted in units of CLDSHAD.BASE — the darkness one cloud lays on this
//     sand — so "a stone's body is 1.6 cloud-shadows deep" is a sentence about this desert.
//   · the LIFT column is counted in units of PROPART.LIFT, and that unit is DERIVED rather than
//     picked: the tumbleweeds' own lit tone #b8a074 IS SAND_COLOR lifted 0.298 of the way to white,
//     to within one level on every channel (184,160,115 computed against 184,160,116 shipped). The
//     desert already answered "what does dry dead matter look like in this sun" at STAGECRAFT #3 and
//     this stone takes the answer rather than inventing a second one. THE DRY BRUSH IS THAT TONE
//     EXACTLY, at 1.00 LIFT, which is right twice over: a tumbleweed IS a bush that came loose.
