  // measurement. `propWobS` averages three neighbours — that is exactly right for a SMOOTH FLANK and exactly
  // wrong for a per-slot index, because averaging pulls every slot toward 0.5: the first cut of this used it
  // and the four skews came out 0.941 to 1.000, a peak shift of under a tenth of a segment. And the index is
  // n+2 rather than 0 because the flank at i=1 already reads propWob(p, 0, ...) through propWobS — reusing it
  // would tie where the dome peaks to how its first shoulder wobbles, which is one die doing two jobs.
  const d = PROPART.SKEW * (propWob(p, n + 2, n) - 0.5) * 2;   // +/- SKEW crown segments, off the slot's own dice
