  //   · HEIGHT is TWO PENS. One pen tall is a line by this notebook's own first rule — *a feature thinner
  //     than the pen is not in the picture* — so the smallest thing that can read as MASS rather than as a
  //     thick stroke is two. Half-height is therefore one pen.
