  //     `sp * w * 0.06`, i.e. ±0.06w, and a root that BINDS them has to be wider than the thing it binds by
  //     the only unit this kind owns. Half-width = 0.06w + pen.
  //   · TONE is `STEMD`, the dark stem, because a root is the shaded end of the same dry matter — and
  //     measured against the ground plate this matters: the plate's own scrub specks average luminance 147.9
  //     and STEMD paints 137.6, so the clump is DARKER than the texture it stands in. (The order says the
  //     brush is "a paler material than the texture" — on the weighted stems that is a 4-level difference and
  //     for STEMD it is the wrong way round. The mass was the defect; the palette was not.)
  //   · IT IS A POLYGON AND NOT A CURVE, AND THAT IS THE INSTRUMENT TALKING. The first cut drew this clump
  //     with two `quadraticCurveTo`s and **`[BRM]` measured it as 0.00px tall.** D128 gave the recorder each
  //     filled path's POINTS, and the criterion that sent this stone reads that as 'a filled root body is
  //     checkable in a sim' — but it books `moveTo`/`lineTo` VERTICES ONLY. A curve's control and end points
  //     are as invisible to it as a stroke is. **A shape built out of what the instrument cannot see is a
  //     shape no law can hold**, so the mound is eight straight segments sampled off the same envelope the
  //     curve had. At 34px tall the silhouette is identical and the body is now assertable.
  //   · AND IT IS THREE PENS TALL, NOT TWO, BECAUSE TWO WAS A FLOOR AND A COLD READER PHOTOGRAPHED IT.
  //     Two pens is what the pen rule licenses as the SMALLEST thing that can read as mass; it is not a target.
  //     At two the reader measured the body at roughly 4.5:1 and called it *"a squashed splat, or a scuff on the
  //     sand … the cure added area and forgot the axis the area needed to be on"* — it merged with the terrain
  //     shading line into one low horizontal smear. Three is the first integer multiple of the pen above a floor
  //     that failed a strangers glance, and the glance is the only instrument that can price this.
