  // RE-USED OBJECT: it arrives here still wearing every field of its previous life. Assign `dust` only
  // when a caller asks for it and the next spark reborn in a dust grain's slot BILLOWS — a phantom puff
  // in the middle of a muzzle flash, spawned by code that never mentioned dust. Every optional field on
  // a pooled record is set on every spawn, or it is a haunting waiting for a busy frame.
  // AND IT IS A DOOR TAG RATHER THAN A FLAG since #79: 0 no dust, 1 the pilot's own feet, 2 THE
  // DOWNWASH. Every reader in the game asks `if (p.dust)` and is untouched by the widening; the two
  // laws that isolate dust from the frame get to isolate ONE door instead of all of them, which is the
  // only reason the number exists. A second boolean field would have been a second haunting.
