// ==== THE DUST FENCE BEGINS (ATMOSPHERE FENCE 2 of 3, cut by #83 THE ONE-WIND AUDIT). THE TWO
//      STREAMS LAW is swept over REGIONS and not over a list of names (#73) — and for four ships
//      this system sat 700 lines OUTSIDE the only region there was. [WND]'s sweep spans the sky's
//      fences alone, while its own comment named "dust, downwash, vultures, set dressing, the
//      shimmer" as inheriting it free: the birds and the furniture do, and these two and the heat
//      band never did. Nothing was rolling the war's dice — measured, not assumed — but the guard
//      was not there, which is one careless editor away from the bug it exists to stop.
//      EVERYTHING DOWN TO THE END FENCE ROLLS dustRand: never Math.random (the war's), never
//      atmRand (the sky's). A dialed system owns its own dice, and owning is neither borrowing nor
//      lending (#78). drawsim [OW] sweeps this region and [MD] rung 10 measures it running. ====
// ======================= THE MOVEMENT DUST (THE-TWO-FIFTY #78) =======================
// THE ORDER: "footstep puffs scaled to speed, landing bursts scaled to fall, dash skids; pooled,
// dialed, desert-toned."
//
// WHAT WAS HERE BEFORE, because this is a REWORK and what it replaces deserves naming. Two emitters,
// both grey, neither of them a puff. A HEEL SPRAY — one #e2e2e2 dot at a flat 22 a second, gated HARD
// at 0.6 x run speed, so it was identical at 0.61x and at 3x and absent one px/s below. A LANDING
// BURST — min(14, impact/120) #d8d8d8 dots, which was honestly scaled to fall and is the one half of
// this order that already existed. And NO dash skids at all. Grey dust on orange sand is the tell of
// an effect authored for the city street and inherited by the desert without anybody looking.
//
// THE THREE DOORS, with one clock behind two of them:
//   · THE STRIDE — footfall puffs, DISTANCE-clocked (below), grains and height on the shear curve.
//   · THE LANDING — one burst at touchdown, its grain count AND its footprint width scaled to impact.
//   · THE SKID — a dash, or the slide the game still calls lethal after it, smears dust BACKWARD off
//     the heel: low, wide, thrown against the direction of travel. A skid is not a footfall — nothing
//     leaves the ground, so nothing plumes.
//
// THE STRIDE DERIVATION, and it is the SPRITE'S number rather than one of mine. ANIM.run is 6 frames
// at 12 fps = 0.500 s per cycle, and a run cycle contains TWO footfalls, so the pilot's feet strike
// the ground 4.00 times a second. At the shipped run speed (P.runSpeed 460 px/s) that is one footfall
// every 115.0 world px — so STRIDE is 115, the puffs land ON THE ANIMATION'S OWN BEAT at run speed,
// and because the clock counts DISTANCE and not time, cadence IS speed everywhere else by
// construction: half speed lays the same trail in space at half the rate in time, a dash lays it 2.7x
// faster. Nothing in that sentence is a taste call, and moving P.runSpeed keeps the beat on the feet.
//
// THE SHEAR CURVE (k), whose floor is the game's own definition of being on the move. Dust needs
// SHEAR — a foot that lifts cleanly raises nothing — and the floor is 40 px/s, which is not a number
// I picked either: it is the exact speed at which the pilot's sprite leaves idle for the run cycle
// (the setAnim ladder in the grounded branch). So k = (|vx| - 40) / (runSpeed - 40): ZERO the instant
// the man stops running, 1.00 at the shipped run speed, 1.43 at 640 px/s (where the game still calls
// his slide a weapon), 2.88 at dash speed, roofed at 3. k scales the grains in a puff and the height
// they climb; the clock scales how often they come. Both rise together, which is why it reads as
// EFFORT instead of as a particle count.
//
// THE SMOKE MACHINE IS THE NAMED FAILURE MODE, so it is bounded four ways instead of trusted:
//   (1) A PEAK ALPHA — a grain is born at DUST.A (0.42) and never at a spark's 1.0.
//   (2) A SHARE OF THE POOL — DUST.SHARE of PBUDGET, enforced at the spawn. The dust may never eat
//       the pool the war's own sparks live in, and because it is a SHARE it tightens automatically
//       with PBUDGET, whatever moves it. drawsim [MD] proves the ceiling BITES at 700 and at 300:
//       an unproven cap is a comment. (The crash guard was the thing that used to move it; since
//       v1.6.679 it does not, so the only writer left is the dial-free constant and the sim.)
//   (3) A PER-FRAME BACKSTOP (DUST.FRAME) — the DAYSHIFT #8 precedent. Deliberately generous, because
//       here it is not a shaping device (there is one pilot, not a crowd): it is the thing that keeps
//       a stalled frame, or #79's downwash joining this pool, from emptying it in one tick.
//   (4) A SHORT LIFE. Dust that hangs is smoke, and the three bounds above are the ones the gate
//       actually holds; this one is here because it is the cheapest of the four to keep.
// THE t^2 FADE IS A LOOK, NOT A BOUND, and that correction is the murder board's ([MD], murder 19). The
// first draft of this table listed the t^2 alpha curve as the fourth thing standing between the dust and
// a silhouette. Then the board rewrote it to a LINEAR fade — the dust hanging at strength for its whole
// life, which is the smoke-machine direction — and every legibility bar in [MD] still passed. So the
// curve earns its place because dust that thins fast and then lingers faint is what suspended sand DOES,
// and not because legibility depends on it. The three that legibility does depend on are the peak alpha,
// the share of the pool, and the height — each with its own rung.
//
// THE TONE IS THE STAGE'S, and this is the order's word "desert-toned" read honestly. What a foot
// kicks up is THE FLOOR IT KICKED, so one pigment is wrong on one of the two stages by definition. On
// the desert the floor is sand — sampled rgb(233,173,87), the mean of the strip a foot can reach —
// and suspended sand SCATTERS light, so the grains are paler than the packed floor they came from. On
// the city the floor is asphalt and the grey the old spray used was RIGHT there; it keeps it. #76's
// lesson is the entire reason this is two palettes instead of one, and [MD] photographs both stages.
//
// AND THE DUST ROLLS ITS OWN DICE — the constitutional half of this stone. THE TWO STREAMS LAW
// (STAGECRAFT #3) moved the atmosphere onto a private stream because a tumbleweed drinking
// Math.random shifted every seed-locked run's COMBAT dice. A DIALED dust is that same crime in
// different clothes: the day DUST can be turned down, a pilot turning it down re-rolls the war. But
// atmRand is not the cure either, and that is the new half — if the pilot's FEET advanced __atmS then
// his pathing would re-roll THE SKY, and every sky law that pins __atmS before measuring (drawsim
// [SS], [DT], [GS]) would quietly stop being deterministic. So the dust takes a THIRD stream of its
// own. THE DOCTRINE, generalised past this system: A DIALED SYSTEM OWNS ITS OWN DICE — its dial may
