  //                  log scale, not the linear one. Area goes as r^2, so r x sqrt(2.95) = 6.18.
  //                  AND IT IS SPENT ON SIZE, NOT COUNT, which is the half a number could not have told
  //                  me: at DUST.M 3 the books read 24 grains and 10.3 levels at p95 and the PHOTOGRAPH
  //                  was still empty (gallery/stone-atmos/zoom/dust-3.png, kept). A 7px dot loses to the
  //                  sand's own pebble texture, which is higher-contrast than any grain of dust; four of
  //                  them are four dots, and twelve are twelve dots. At 6.2 the same four overlap into
  //                  ONE soft mass about 27px across — a puff, which is the thing the order asked for.
  //                  The count, the cadence, the alpha ceiling and all four of #78's bounds are untouched.
  RISE: 46,        // a grain's upward speed at k = 1, px/s — about 8px of climb over its life, and
  //                  about 35px at the shear roof, which is mid-shin on this sprite.
  LIFE: 0.5,       // seconds. Short by design: dust that hangs is smoke.
  A: 0.42,         // THE PEAK ALPHA, and the first of the four bounds. A spark is born opaque.
  //                  **#290 TRIED TO RAISE THIS AND THE GAME'S OWN LAW REFUSED, WHICH IS THE FINDING.**
  //                  `particles` has ranked #1 by screen-time since v1.6.598 and the tour's cold reader
