  // MEASURED BEFORE BEING DESCRIBED, because my first draft of this comment said "in every desert
  // frame" and that was not true. Swept over 200 camera positions x 30 times: a mean of 2.03 of the six
  // were on screen, 48% of samples held at least one and 16.3% held all six — and the 52% that held
  // NONE is its own bug, because JS's % returns a negative remainder, so the whole left-hand cohort of
