  //   row where far sand meets near sand IS a drawn line. #214 named this from an 8x still. #215 and this
  //   stone's first cut both went after the ART instead, and the art was innocent: a fresh sub-reader,
  //   given only the frames, measured the bar ACROSS FOUR RUNNING FRAMES and found mean |dL| of 0.52-1.11
  //   where the sand beside it moved 5.7-18.9. **A row of ground that stays put while the ground moves is
  //   drawn, not terrain** — and it then showed the bar's RGB is the haze row above it scaled by 0.8872,
