  grudge: 'THE GRUDGE: the flying bomb’s page — how far it looks, how fast it commits, how long the fuse burns, and how wide the blast reaches. KIN RADIUS is wider than BLAST RADIUS on purpose: it is deadlier to its own family than to you. Try: KIN DAMAGE 2, deploy six — the chain stops.',
  treasure: 'THE VAULT: the fountain’s own page — the beats a payout runs through, the shape of its flight home, the arrival music, and the combo that chains a mow into one river. Every dial here changes how a payout FEELS, never what it is WORTH. Try: drop FOUNTAIN HANG to zero and watch a big kill stop being readable.',
  deploy: 'The deploy desk: build a wave by hand. Every family has a COUNT (nothing spawns until DEPLOY THE WAVE), plus HP/SPD/AGG/SIZE cells that price the bodies it mints; the cards below stage the street, the dream, and five theater drills. Try: JACKBOY 6, DEPLOY THE WAVE.',
  armory: 'The armory: your own arsenal, rung by rung — every weapon and aura ladder with live values, free to wear. Steps go through the real buy paths and the loadout vault remembers across deaths. Try: tap an upgrade’s name for its note, then RESET ALL for a clean bench.',
  sky: 'The dream war: tears pour drone storms, popcorn schools around platinum diamonds, and the cloud shoots as one pooled volley. These dials govern the pour, the mix, the appetite, the chain fuse, and the swarm’s geometry. Try: DREAM WAVE on the deploy desk, then POUR RATE and DIVE CAP here.',
  street: 'The street war: jack boys press in squads, feint, and break. These few dials are the street’s temperament — focus budget, stand-off distance, chatter, and the poker (feints, retreats, bails). Try: AGGRO 3× against a deployed squad and feel the block turn.',
  dealer: 'Watch Dealer 2: the coward with product — he closes slow, throws at range, blocks once with the case, and runs faster than he came. Every number of the kite loop is a dial here, most flagged as bold guesses awaiting the tuning flight. Try: deal one dealer, then move RETREAT SPEED and THROW RANGE.',
  lion: 'The sky lion: a bolted-down head that learned to hunt. These dials are the whole of that brain \u2014 where it stands, how fast it takes ground, how far it may stray, and how far ahead of you it aims. Try: THE PATIENCE at 0 and again at 60 \u2014 the same sky, fired at every chance or almost never.',
  rabbi: 'The priesthood: floating priests on a seat ledger, telegraphed beams under fire and beam budgets, eight personalities over one brain. These dials are that brain — aim, spacing, budgets, the commit clock, the hunted read, the cage. Try: THE SCENARIO DECK below (2-DUEL first), then FIRE BUDGET.',
  // THE PAGE PREFACE THAT NAMED TWO DOORS AND HAD NEITHER (cured v1.6.458). This line has told the pilot to
