      // thrown away the one piece of design in the old array to gain nothing.
      const AUD_LEAD = ['arrive', 'laser', 'zap', 'boom', 'slash', 'slashHit', 'kill', 'hurt', 'jbWind', 'jbStab', 'rbCharge', 'jump', 'dash', 'gem', 'pendant', 'clink', 'lock', 'shieldBreak', 'przRapid', 'przFreeze', 'przHeart', 'przSlow', 'przOver', 'przDecoy', 'decoyPop', 'przGold', 'przGtouch', 'przMiss', 'przAmmo', 'wallyKill', 'wallyShield', 'wallyPip', 'wallyDown'];
      // THE ARGUMENT MAP. Every button used to call its voice as `SFX[name](player.x)`, and for the twelve
      // voices whose first parameter is NOT a position that was simply wrong — `hit` was auditioned with
      // `dmg = player.x` (a five-figure damage number, saved only by its own `Math.min(1.6, …)` clamp),
      // `stinger` with a cue name of `14320`, `combo`/`lock`/`gem` at absurd ladder rungs. They played, so
      // nobody noticed. **A voice auditioned with the wrong arguments is not auditioned**, which is the same
      // sentence this file already wrote about voices with no button at all.
