// (#120) THE HYPE BAR — the announcer's band, and a FIRST-CLASS HUD PIECE rather than a fourth announce floater.
//  **THE NAME IS `hypebar` BECAUSE `banner` IS TAKEN.** `WRUN.bannerT` and `WMODE.screen === 'banner'` are the
//  wave-mode intermission SCREEN (11 hits), and `herald` is the exhibit hall's (16). A `hudRect('banner', …)` piece
//  would have shared a furniture key with a screen state, which is the collision the amendment caught before I built it.
//
//  **EVERY NUMBER IS DERIVED FROM THE MEASURED MAP OR FROM THE GRAMMAR IT EXTENDS:**
//   · `H 58` is `drawExhibHerald`'s own band height, reused rather than re-picked — one letterbox height in this game.
//   · `Y 282` is FOUR PIXELS under `ticker`'s floor, and `ticker` is the lowest-reaching zone the furniture map holds
//     (`y136 + (5*26+12) = 278`). Nothing else registers below it, so this is the first free band and not a taste call.
//   · `W 800` is `announce`'s 660 plus 140. A banner that outranks a callout must READ as a different object, and the
