    //   reader measured the teaching ring against the desert sky: sky rgb(171,205,205), stroke at its
    //   brightest rgb(190,202,187) — **a luminance delta of 0.7 out of 255.** Geometrically perfect,
    //   perceptually absent: *"decoration by measurement, not by taste"*, and it did not register on the
    //   reader's first pass at full size. `hold` is opt-in and means "this ring is a STATEMENT about a
    //   distance", so a statement now carries an outline that survives any background it is drawn over.
    //   **THE SAME READER'S OTHER RING FINDING WAS REFUTED WITH ARITHMETIC AND THE RECEIPT BELONGS HERE:**
    //   it measured the ring plateauing at 145-150px and called it a 13-15% under-teach of the 170px kill
    //   radius. `WORLD_ZOOM = 0.85` and **170 x 0.85 = 144.5** — the ring is at exactly `SUI.BLAST_R` in
    //   WORLD units, and the damage it teaches is charged in those same units, so both scale together and a
