  //
  // Pass two passed nine of eleven graded conditions and was still REJECTED on the only one that
  // matters: *"it reads as something big and made of glass broke, AND THE WORLD DID NOT NOTICE."* The
  // reader's diagnosis was exact and it is not about the effect at all: *"the star field, the ground
  // wireframe, the horizon and the player are exactly as dark at the peak of the blowout as before it.
  // A 300-unit crystal blowing out at 12,000 ft lights nothing but itself... a stranger judges scale by
  // what a thing does to EVERYTHING ELSE, not by how many pieces come off it."*
  //
  // **PRIOR ART, AND IT IS THIS EXACT SEAM: `SETDUSK`'s closing grade, eight lines up** — *"one full-stage
  // grade over the WORLD, under every letter of the HUD, drawn at the exact world/screen seam so nothing
  // gameplay darkens unevenly and nothing written dims at all."* Same transform, same rect, same place in
  // the pass; it lifts instead of dropping, and it is `lighter` because light ARRIVING is added.
